[block'ORD-0043-item-scheme'
  [ref'EMS']
  [ctx'the naming scheme of the Regent, 2026-10-15','.guidelines/.orders/INTAKE-EFFECTS.md, section 9.1']
  [ctx'the measured proposal and the answers of the Regent','.guidelines/.orders/INTAKE-EFFECTS.md, sections 11 and 12']
  [ctx'the case that exists to prove it','conformance/README.md, E-06']
  [tgt'step 5 of the trail to the final Explorer: the emitted document says which root an item belongs to and where it sits in its queue, root-x on the root of a series of items and x-item-## on each item, in both engines']
  [ins'write origin on the head of each chain and each holds that has items, root-x, and on each item after it, x-item-##, numbered from 01 with two digits and three past 99, x the head own name, its binds, or its element name']
  [ins'read both ways back past it, the attribute being derived from position']
  [ins'state the attribute in PACKAGE_TARGET.md and XML_REFERENCE.md, and enter E-06 into conformance']
  [cnst'only a root that has items carries root-x; join and chain keep what they do']
  [cnst'the xml hashes of the declared sources with items move by decision, and no other hash moves']
  [cnst'npm run check and npm run check:rust green']
  [val'the engines','every source of the snapshot answers the same XML in the Rust as in the JS, the moved hashes named, and the scheme seen failing before the code']
];
